// A binary literal takes no suffix. At `0b1i` the longest match is the INT
// `0b1`, because `i` is not a binary digit, and `i` is a name, so the program
// has a name directly after a literal, a syntax error (spec/01-lexical.md, row
// `suffix-boundary`). A scanner that reads an optional `i` after each literal
// accepts it.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). The first line
// prints `ran`, so an implementation that finds the error only when it runs
// the program prints `ran` and fails this probe.

print "ran";
print 0b1i;

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
// COVERS: literal suffix-boundary
